then in 2007 I think I gave a TED talk I think was 2007 and it was on the psychology of evil It was one of the most popular talks of how many millions of people have seen it but at the end of the talk I said I raised the concerns issue of we now know how easy it is for good people to be seduced into doing evil. But I said to the audience, do you think it's possible that we can inspire and even train ordinary people to become heroes? And it hit a responsive court. And that's, I had, I just wanted to have a dramatic ending to the talk. Many people in the audience came up, including Al Gore, Pierre Omidyar, the person started

